<section class="mt-12 max-w-3xl space-y-5">
  <p>
    Households schooling on their own terms have to produce evidence: a
    portfolio, an hours log, something transcript-shaped, an account of what
    was covered. What usually happens is a fortnight of panic each year,
    reconstructing a whole year's learning from memory and a shoebox.
  </p>
  <p>
    The reconstruction is unnecessary. If mastery was being recorded as it
    was earned, the record already exists — it just needs printing.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="mt-14">
  <h2 class="display text-2xl">What it can produce</h2>
  <div class="mt-6 grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
    <%= render Ui::CardComponent.new(title: "A portfolio") do %>
      <p class="text-sm text-soft">
        What was actually covered and the work that showed it, per subject,
        across the period — assembled from evidence recorded at the time
        rather than remembered afterwards.
      </p>
    <% end %>
    <%= render Ui::CardComponent.new(title: "An hours log") do %>
      <p class="text-sm text-soft">
        Where hours are what your jurisdiction counts. Built from sessions
        that were logged as they happened, which is the only way this number
        is ever honest.
      </p>
    <% end %>
    <%= render Ui::CardComponent.new(title: "Something transcript-shaped") do %>
      <p class="text-sm text-soft">
        For the older learner who will eventually need to hand somebody a
        document. Subjects, coverage, and what was demonstrated.
      </p>
    <% end %>
    <%= render Ui::CardComponent.new(title: "A progress account") do %>
      <p class="text-sm text-soft">
        In plain language, for the conversation with a relative, an
        assessor, or the learner themselves about how the year went.
      </p>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="mt-14 max-w-3xl">
  <h2 class="display text-2xl">It reports, it doesn't embellish</h2>
  <p class="mt-4 text-soft">
    The generated record says what the year's evidence supports. It won't
    inflate coverage, invent hours, or describe mastery that was never
    demonstrated — partly because that would be dishonest, and partly
    because a record like that is worse than useless the moment anybody
    checks it.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="mt-14 max-w-3xl">
  <h2 class="display text-2xl">Requirements differ, and it says so</h2>
  <p class="mt-4 text-soft">
    What a household must produce, and to whom, varies enormously by where
    you live, and changes. The app generates the documents; it does not tell
    you what your jurisdiction requires, and where that matters it says to
    check rather than asserting a rule it can't stand behind.
  </p>
</section>
